 "duration": 50.78,
 "text": "You don't need more willpower to stop checking your phone, you need more distance. When it's on your desk, checking it takes one second, so your hand gets there before you've even decided to. So for your first focused block, put your phone in another room and close the door, then set a timer on your laptop for 25 minutes. Now checking it means standing up and walking away from your work, and that small pause is usually enough to keep you on the task. Studying one chapter phone in the kitchen, writing a report, the first page phone in the bedroom. When the timer ends, take 5 minutes. Check whatever you want, then start the next block. So before your next block, pick the room your phone goes to. One closed door does more than willpower ever will. That's what Demure is for. You archive your dream today so you can see it tomorrow and break it down into small steps you can actually do. If you want to try it out, I've put the link in the bio.",
